Add a ScriptMgr hook for scaling threat a unit generates.

Touches: src/server/game/Combat/ThreatManager.cpp,
src/server/game/Scripting/ScriptDefines/UnitScript.h,
src/server/game/Scripting/ScriptDefines/UnitScript.cpp,
src/server/game/Scripting/ScriptMgr.h

Why: report #91 -- "Add 1000% aggro gen on warrior protection perk, can't
keep anything attacking me as tank because everyone hits too hard."

There was no script hook anywhere in the threat pipeline, so the module had
no way to multiply a Protection warrior's threat. The cleanest insertion
point is the bottom of ThreatManager::AddThreat, right after the engine's
own modifiers (spell threat entries, SPELLMOD_THREAT, school modifiers)
have been applied to `amount` -- at that point `target` is the unit
generating the threat and `_owner` is the unit holding the list.

New hook, mirroring the existing OnCreatureLevelForTarget pattern
(core-patch 0025):

  UnitScript (virtual, default no-op):
    virtual void OnCalculateThreat(Unit* attacker, Unit* victim,
        float& threat, SpellInfo const* spell) { }

  - UNITHOOK_ON_CALCULATE_THREAT added to the UnitScript hook enum before
    UNITHOOK_END.
  - ScriptMgr::OnCalculateThreat forward declared in ScriptMgr.h.
  - CALL_ENABLED_HOOKS dispatch in UnitScript.cpp.
  - sScriptMgr->OnCalculateThreat(target, _owner, amount, spell) called in
    ThreatManager::AddThreat after CalculateModifiedThreat, gated on
    !ignoreModifiers.

The module consumes it: LivingGearClassPerksUnit overrides OnCalculateThreat
and multiplies threat by 11 for players with the Protection warrior perk
(SPELL_WARRIOR_PROTECTION). Fires for melee, spell, periodic and heal threat
alike because it sits at the bottom of AddThreat. All four hook parts are
present (enum, virtual, forward, dispatch), so the hook actually fires.
